      "description": "Native radio picker; selected soft-indigo surface and visible group focus. Schematics are decorative.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-choice\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"family\" checked>Cabinets</label>",
      "css": ".ds-choice{display:block;position:relative;padding:18px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border,#2D2D4E);border-radius:10px;font:550 14px var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif;color:var(--text-primary,#F9FAFB);cursor:pointer;transition:border-color 150ms,background-color 150ms}.ds-choice:has(input:checked){border-color:var(--accent,#6366F1);background:var(--accent-soft,#24223F)}.ds-choice:focus-within{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#A5B4FC);outline-offset:3px}.ds-choice input{width:17px;height:17px;accent-color:var(--accent-button,#4F46E5)}.ds-choice:has(input:disabled){opacity:.65;cursor:not-allowed}@media(max-width:540px){.ds-choice{padding:18px 12px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Draft name field",
      "kind": "input",
      "description": "Shared creation/inline rename control; 46px minimum height, invalid border and mobile entry size.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-name\">Project name<input value=\"Hallway shoe rack\"></label>",
      "css": ".ds-name{display:block;font:550 14px var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif;color:var(--text-primary,#F9FAFB)}.ds-name input{display:block;width:100%;margin-top:12px;min-height:46px;border:1px solid var(--border,#2D2D4E);border-radius:7px;padding:10px 12px;background:var(--bg-base,#0F0F1A);color:inherit;caret-color:var(--accent-text,#A5A0FF);font:400 14px var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif}.ds-name input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#A5B4FC);outline-offset:5px}.ds-name input[aria-invalid=true]{border-color:var(--danger-text,#FCA5A5)}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-name input{font-size:16px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Browser draft card",
      "kind": "card",
      "description": "Name/type/date preview; runtime adds a family schematic and separate Rename/Delete controls.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-draft\"><a href=\"#\"><h3>Hallway shoe rack</h3><p>Shoe rack / Browser draft</p><time>Edited 21 Oct 2026</time></a></article>",
      "css": ".ds-draft{border:1px solid var(--border,#2D2D4E);border-radius:12px;overflow:clip;min-width:0;font-family:var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif;color:var(--text-primary,#F9FAFB)}.ds-draft a{display:block;padding:20px;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.ds-draft a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#A5B4FC);outline-offset:-4px}.ds-draft h3{margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:550;line-height:1.45;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-draft p,.ds-draft time{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted,#9CA3AF)}.ds-draft p{margin:7px 0 12px}.ds-draft time{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Destructive confirmation",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Visual content preview. Runtime native showModal provides Cancel-first focus, idle Escape dismissal and trigger restoration; CSS alone does not implement these.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-confirm\"><h2>Delete this draft?</h2><p>This draft will be removed from this browser.</p><div><button>Cancel</button><button class=\"ds-danger\">Delete draft</button></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-confirm{width:min(440px,calc(100vw - 40px));padding:28px;border:1px solid var(--border,#2D2D4E);border-radius:12px;background:var(--bg-surface,#1A1A2E);color:var(--text-primary,#F9FAFB);font-family:var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif;max-height:calc(100dvh - 40px);overflow-y:auto}.ds-confirm h2{margin:0;font-size:21px;font-weight:550}.ds-confirm p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--text-muted,#9CA3AF);margin-top:14px}.ds-confirm div{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:24px}.ds-confirm button{padding:10px 16px;min-height:40px;border:1px solid var(--border,#2D2D4E);border-radius:7px;background:var(--bg-surface,#1A1A2E);color:inherit;font:550 12px var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 150ms,color 150ms}.ds-confirm button:hover{background:var(--bg-elevated,#252540)}.ds-confirm button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#A5B4FC);outline-offset:5px}.ds-confirm .ds-danger{border:0;background:var(--danger-fill,#B91C1C);color:white}.ds-confirm .ds-danger:hover{background:#991B1B}.ds-confirm button:disabled{opacity:.75;cursor:not-allowed}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-confirm button{min-height:44px}}@media(max-width:540px){.ds-confirm{padding:24px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Storage recovery notice",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Preserves unreadable/newer data; runtime adds wrapping Retry, recovery-download and confirmed Reset actions. Unavailable storage offers Retry.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-storage\"><h2>Your saved drafts could not be read.</h2><p>The existing data has been left untouched. Download a recovery copy before choosing to reset it.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-storage{border:1px solid var(--border,#2D2D4E);border-radius:10px;padding:24px;margin:20px 0;color:var(--text-primary,#F9FAFB);font-family:var(--font-inter,Inter),sans-serif}.ds-storage h2{font-size:17px;font-weight:550;margin:0}.ds-storage p{font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted,#9CA3AF);line-height:1.65;max-width:70ch;margin-top:8px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The calm furniture workspace",
    "overview": "CutPlan Studio uses the supplied master palette and a restrained creative-tool shell. Indigo identifies navigation, actions and furniture geometry; neutral surfaces keep ordinary tasks readable. The product remains a calm workspace.\n\nThis record describes the Phase 1 Home, Projects and Orders foundation, extended by the Phase 2 guest draft workflow. Visual authority remains [the design requirement](docs/requirements/03_Design_Specification.md), derived from the owner's master. Composition and implementation differences belong in [the foundation note](docs/design/phase-01-foundation.md); requirements remain separate under docs/requirements.",
    "donts": [
      "Don't imply the schematic is a saved design or production drawing.",
      "Don't introduce decorative gradients, repeated shadows or animated badges into this workspace.",
      "Don't present later-phase controls as established Phase 1 components."
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the master's paired palettes and role-specific contrast adjustments.",
      "Do use sentence case, Inter, visible focus and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "Do keep furniture schematics unnumbered until real design measurements exist.",
      "Do show true empty states and explain unavailable actions."
    ],
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Paired dark and light themes.",
      "Self-hosted Inter and compact sentence-case typography.",
      "Flat bordered surfaces and geometric furniture linework.",
      "Honest empty states and explicit unavailable actions."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The accent roles rule",
        "body": "Keep the master indigo for geometry; use accessible text and button derivatives for their respective roles.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The quiet hierarchy rule",
        "body": "Reserve the largest type for the introductory furniture message; navigation and supporting copy remain compact and readable.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The flat surface rule",
        "body": "Use tonal separation and fine borders rather than shadows to establish depth.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ]
  }
